Pseudo Code

Setting the game score to 0 and creating a 2D 
array to store the game scores. 


Creating the game scores menu to explain the directions 
to the user while also receiving their input to save, 
compare, display, and sort the game scores.


If the user chooses A
The user will enter teams score
The user will enter opponents score
The score will be saved and the games will
be increased by one. 

If the user chooses B
The program will go through all the games
The program will compare our score to the opponents score
The program will count the wins, losses, and ties
The current record will be displayed

If the user chooses C
The program will go through all the games
The program will check if our score is higher than the opponents score
If we won the game, the scores will be displayed
If there are no wins, a message will be displayed

If the user chooses D
The game scores will be copied into a separate array
The program will use bubble sort to compare the opponents scores
If one opponents score is higher than the next score
The scores will be swapped
This will keep going until the scores are from lowest to highest
All of the sorted game results will be displayed

If the user chooses E
The program will exit

If the user enters anything else
An invalid choice message will be displayed

The menu will keep running until the user chooses E


